Raygun for FreeBSD (x86_64), built from source in a FreeBSD VM by the release workflow's freebsd
job (run by hand while it's experimental; see docs/PLATFORMS.md).

It needs WebKitGTK 4.1 and GStreamer's plugins for sound and video:

    pkg install webkit2-gtk_41 gstreamer1-plugins-good gstreamer1-plugins-bad gstreamer1-libav

Then run ./raygun from this folder. Raygun keeps its data in a raygun-data folder beside it (or
in the folder RAYGUN_HOME names). To have it in the desktop's menus:

    install -m 755 raygun /usr/local/bin/raygun
    install -m 644 raygun.desktop /usr/local/share/applications/raygun.desktop
    install -m 644 raygun.png /usr/local/share/icons/hicolor/128x128/apps/raygun.png

Installed under /usr/local, Raygun keeps its data in ~/.local/share/app.raygun.player.
